{#
  Render files_report_entries for one host as plain text lines.

  Layout mechanics (column-0 block tags, plain ASCII, why not colour) are
  the same as the other two reports' templates - see
  roles/toolchain_report/templates/toolchain-report.j2 for the rationale.

  The two sections read differently, which is why they are sections. A
  single entry is one line of config and one file, so an operator can check
  it against the config by eye. A bulk entry is one line of config and an
  unknown number of files, so the run is the ONLY place its expansion is
  visible - hence the matched files are grouped under the pattern that
  named them, with a count. Forty JAR paths with no pattern above them do
  not tell an operator which line of config to go and edit.

  A group is per PATTERN, not per declared entry, so one glob declared
  twice with two targetDirs renders as a single group listing both
  landings. Its count therefore reads "landed", not "matched": the question
  the report answers is which files reached the VM and where, not how many
  lines of config asked for them - and every landing is printed either way.

  The header counts statuses only, like both sibling reports. A total would
  be the sum of the two numbers beside it, and the count that is not
  derivable from config - how far a glob expanded - belongs on the pattern
  it expanded from, not in a play-wide total.

  Ordering is stable without sorting anything here: groupby sorts by the
  grouping key, and within a group the rows keep accumulator order - each
  declaration's matches, already sorted by source path during resolution.
#}
{% set entries = files_report_entries | default([]) %}
{% set copied = entries | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'copied') | list %}
{% set unchanged = entries | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'unchanged') | list %}
{% set singles = entries | selectattr('origin', 'equalto', 'single') | list %}
{% set bulk = entries | selectattr('origin', 'equalto', 'bulk') | list %}
Files report for {{ inventory_hostname }} -- {{ copied | length }} copied, {{ unchanged | length }} unchanged
{% if not entries %}
  (no file entries were declared - nothing was copied here)
{% endif %}
{% if singles %}
section 1 - named files (one declared entry, one file)
{% for entry in singles %}
  {{ "%-9s" | format(entry.status) }} {{ entry.target }}  {{ entry.owner }}:{{ entry.group }} {{ entry.mode }}
      source  {{ entry.source }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if bulk %}
section 2 - glob matched files (one declared entry, every file it named)
{% for pattern, rows in bulk | groupby('pattern') %}
  pattern {{ pattern }} -- {{ rows | length }} landed
{% for entry in rows %}
    {{ "%-9s" | format(entry.status) }} {{ entry.target }}  {{ entry.owner }}:{{ entry.group }} {{ entry.mode }}
        source  {{ entry.source }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
